           <li>{{ city }}: {{ items|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}</li>
         {% endfor %}</ul>
 
+    By default the groups are sorted in ascending order of the
+    attribute. Pass ``reverse=True`` to sort the groups in descending
+    order instead, for example to list the newest or highest values
+    first.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for year, items in posts|groupby("year", reverse=true) %}
+          <li>{{ year }}: {{ items|map(attribute="title")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    You can pass a callable as ``key_transform`` to change how each
+    group's key is displayed, for example to format a date. The
+    callable is applied only to the key that is yielded, after the
+    items have been sorted and grouped by the original attribute value,
+    so it never changes which items end up together. It combines with
+    ``reverse``, which only controls the order of the groups.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        {% for month, items in events|groupby("date", key_transform=fmt) %}
+          <li>{{ month }}: {{ items|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``key_transform`` parameter.
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``reverse`` parameter.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
